    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player to achieve the winning condition through strategic play of cards.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Setup: prepare players, deck or tiles, and opening layout according to the variant. 2. Turn loop: each player performs one legal action (play, capture, build, bet, or pass/draw as applicable). 3. Resolution: each action updates control of tricks/cards/pot/layout. 4. End condition: when hand-ending criteria are met, scoring is computed and match state advances.',
      'Scoring example: Card points are counted using Briscola values (Ace 11, Three 10, King 4, Queen 3, Jack 2; others 0). In Briscola a 31, play stops as soon as a player claims to have at least 31 points in their tricks; if the claim is correct they win, and if it is incorrect the opponent wins the hand. First player to correctly claim 31 or more card points in their tricks wins the hand; an incorrect claim immediately gives the win to the opponent..',
